-- g8-tests-red: tests that are MEANT to fail, nineteen of them, one per fork.
-- Each asserts, of the FAVOURED interpretation, the answer that the OTHER reading of the fork would give on the fork's discriminating case.  The favoured interpretation gives the opposite answer, so each
-- assertion fails.  They are the proof that the harness can fail, and the proof that each fork bites: if one of them ever passes, the two readings of that fork no longer differ on its discriminating case.
-- check.sh expects exactly nineteen failed assertions here, no refused one, and no other error.

§ `Tests meant to fail: the other reading's answer, asked of the favoured interpretation`

-- F8.1.  Notice 1 February 2026, document provided 20 February 2026, proceedings commenced 10 February 2027.  The other reading keeps it only to 1 February 2027.
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) the Commissioner may keep the document until` `the favoured interpretation` `T26 retention, proceedings commenced on 10 February 2027 and not concluded` EQUALS `retention is permitted up to and including` (YMD 2027 2 1)

-- F8.2.  Request 1 May 2026, copy supplied 20 May 2026, seven days: the other reading says it was not supplied in time.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(6) the copy was supplied as soon as practicable` `the favoured interpretation` `T26 a request for a copy, copy supplied on 20 May 2026` (JUST 7) TRUE

-- F8.3.  A humanist association: the other reading says it meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c).
#ASSERT `Art 28(1)(a) the charity meets the charity test by virtue of Article 6(1)(c)` `the favoured interpretation` TRUE FALSE `T28 a humanist association`

-- F8.4.  A registered charity's refused request for the restricted section: the other reading gives it an appeal by analogy with 33(1)(b).
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 restricted section` `T33 refuses` TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal by analogy with Article 33(1)(b)`

-- F8.5.  A party whose complaint is that the tribunal's decision was wrong in law: the other reading lets it appeal to the court.
#ASSERT `Art 35(1) the party may appeal to the court` `the favoured interpretation` TRUE FALSE (`Ground alleged in an appeal` WITH `standard alleged` IS `wrong`, `respect alleged` IS `the law`)

-- F8.6.  Decision 1 January 2026, notice 10 January 2026, 30 days, lodged 5 February 2026: the other reading says the appeal was late.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 36(2) the appeal is in time` `the favoured interpretation` `T36 an appeal lodged on 5 February 2026` `T36 a limit of 30 days`

-- F8.7.  Fourteen days from service on 1 June 2026: the other reading counts the day of service, so the last day is 14 June.
#ASSERT `Art 26(1) the last day allowed by the notice` `the favoured interpretation` `T26 a period of fourteen days` `T26 the first of June 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 14

-- F8.8.  Three months from 30 November 2027 is 91 days (to 29 February 2028): the days reading says 91 days is over the maximum.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26 and 29 a term of imprisonment is within the maximum` `the favoured interpretation` `the offence of contravening a requirement under Article 26(1) or (4)` (YMD 2027 11 30) 91

-- F8.9.  A year from 20 February 2026: the other reading ends it the day before the anniversary, on 19 February 2027.
#ASSERT `Art 26(5)(a) the last day of the retention year` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 2 20) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 19

-- F8.10.  A year from 29 February 2028: the other reading ends it on 1 March 2029.
#ASSERT `Art 26(5)(a) the last day of the retention year` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2029 3 1

-- F8.11.  Received from another recipient, disclosed with the consent of the person it relates to only: the other reading says no offence.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 29(1) the person commits an offence` `the favoured interpretation` FALSE `T29 information received from a person who received it under the Law` `T29 a disclosure with the consent of the person it relates to`

-- F8.12.  Thirty days from 10 January 2026: the other reading counts the first day, so the last day is 8 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Art 36(2) the last day to bring the appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T36 an appeal lodged on 5 February 2026` 30 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 8

-- F8.13.  Another registered charity with an interest in a similar name: the other reading gives it an appeal under 33(5)(b).
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 another registered charity with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5)(b)`

-- F8.14.  The Commissioner believes there has been misconduct, but the facts do not bear it out: the other reading says there is no ground.
#ASSERT `T27 the grounds, on the reading and with the facts` `the favoured interpretation` TRUE (LIST `T27 belief (a)`) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS EMPTY

-- F8.15.  A notice on the ground of the charity's own misconduct: the other reading lets its steps include removing a governor.
#ASSERT `Art 27(4) the steps may include suspension, removal or replacement` `the favoured interpretation` `T27 belief (a)` FALSE

-- F8.16.  A deregistration granted on the charity's own application: the other reading gives no appeal.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a registered charity` `T33 deregister on application` `T33 does` TRUE EQUALS `no appeal is given by Part 8`

-- F8.17.  A person who was a governor only before the entity was registered: the other reading says the person is not within Article 26(2)(b).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `the favoured interpretation` `T26 a governor of an entity before it was registered`

-- F8.18.  The charity test failed at the application only, the name undesirable at the appeal only: the other reading gives an appeal on grounds that differ between the two times.
#ASSERT `T33 the right of appeal at the two times` `the favoured interpretation` `T33 a stranger with an interest in the name` `T33 register` `T33 does` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `a right of appeal under Article 33(5) on grounds that differ between the two times`

-- F8.19.  An employee of a formerly registered entity: the other reading lets the Commissioner require an explanation of the document from the employee.
#ASSERT `Art 26(4)(a) an explanation of the document may be required of the person` `the favoured interpretation` `T26 an employee of a formerly registered entity`
